P3
========

🔹 Problem Statement:
In a SAML identity provider (IdP) configuration, users may be members of groups from multiple sources:

Internal users with DNs like cn=ODS_<GroupName>,... (from OpenDJ)

External users with DNs like cn=AAD_<GroupName>,... (from AzureAD)

The goal is to write an OGNL expression that:

Retrieves all group DNs from thee two Directory Servers

Parses each DN to extract the Common Name (CN) component.

Identifies groups that start with either ODS_ or AAD_.

Adds these group names to a single list.

Returns a single SAML attribute (AttributeValue) containing all the relevant group names.
 
 
Solution:


#roles = new java.util.ArrayList(),

// Fetching Internal user groups from ODS Directory
#internalGroups = #this.get("ds.ODS.isMemberOf") != null ? #this.get("ds.ODS.isMemberOf").getValues() : {},
#internalGroups.{
    #dn = #this,
    #ldapName = new javax.naming.ldap.LdapName(#dn),
    #cn = #ldapName.getRdn(#group.size() - 1).getValue().toString(),
    #roles.add(#cn)
},

// Fetching External user groups from AAD
#externalGroups = #this.get("ds.AAD.isMemberOf") != null ? #this.get("ds.AAD.isMemberOf").getValues() : {},
#externalGroups.{
    #dn = #this,
    #ldapName = new javax.naming.ldap.LdapName(#dn),
    #cn = #ldapName.getRdn(#group.size() - 1).getValue().toString(),
    #roles.add(#cn)
},

new org.sourceid.saml20.adapter.attribute.AttributeValue(#roles)
